`lazy` as the first token stores the query PLAN under a name, not a table - nothing touches the file yet
extend the plan by re-assigning the binding - still lazy, still no execution
reading a lazy binding without collecting just prints its (optimised) plan
SELECT [col("sym"), col("side"), col("price"), col("size"), (col("price") * col("size").cast(Float64)).alias("notional")]
  Parquet SCAN [examples/data/trades.parquet]
  PROJECT 4/5 COLUMNS
  SELECTION: col("size") > 100
  ESTIMATED ROWS: 8
`collect` runs the plan once and binds the result as a normal in-memory table
shape: (1, 2)
┌──────┬──────────┐
│ sym  ┆ notional │
│ ---  ┆ ---      │
│ str  ┆ f64      │
╞══════╪══════════╡
│ MSFT ┆ 124800.0 │
└──────┴──────────┘
`cols` always resolves to a table, even on a lazy binding
shape: (5, 2)
┌──────────┬───────┐
│ column   ┆ dtype │
│ ---      ┆ ---   │
│ str      ┆ str   │
╞══════════╪═══════╡
│ notional ┆ f64   │
│ side     ┆ str   │
│ size     ┆ i64   │
│ sym      ┆ str   │
│ …        ┆ …     │
└──────────┴───────┘
